9 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 9\n4 4 9 3 3 3 3 3 9 3 3 3 3 9 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 9 9\n4 4 4 3 3 9 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 9 3 9 9 3 9 3 9 3 3 9 4\n4 4 4 9 9 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 9 4 4 4\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-0dc63919\nTest input (3x27):\n8 8 8 8 5 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 5 8 8 8 8 5 8 8 8 8 8 5 8 8\n8 5 5 8 8 8 8 8 5 8 8 5 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 5 8 8 8 8 8 8 8\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 5 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 5 8 8 5 8 8 8\nWrong attempts used: 0/8. Demo requests used: 3/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    marker = 5\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Fill the gaps between markers on each row and column.\n    for r in range(h):\n        cols = [c for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == marker]\n        for a, b in zip(cols, cols[1:]):\n            for c in range(a + 1, b):\n                out[r][c] = 3\n\n    for c in range(w):\n        rows = [r for r in range(h) if grid[r][c] == marker]\n        for a, b in zip(rows, rows[1:]):\n            for r in range(a + 1, b):\n                out[r][c] = 3\n\n    # Fill gaps along 45-degree diagonals as well.\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] != marker:\n                continue\n            for dr, dc in ((1, 1), (1, -1)):\n                rr, cc = r + dr, c + dc\n                while 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w:\n                    if grid[rr][cc] == marker:\n                        steps = abs(rr - r)\n                        for k in range(1, steps):\n                            out[r + dr * k][c + dc * k] = 3\n                        break\n                    rr += dr\n                    cc += dc\n\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":96,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793553565.441,"t1":1793553579.911,"alias":"task-0dc63919","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n7